{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
	<p><code>apply</code> renders its content, then runs the result through one or more filters.</p>

	{% apply example(context: { name: "ada" }) %}
		{% verbatim %}
{% apply upper|trim %}
	Hello, {{ name }}
{% endapply %}
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<p>The content was escaped as it rendered. The built-in text filters, such as <code>upper</code> and <code>replace</code>, keep it safe and change only its text, so it isn't escaped twice. Text they add, such as a replacement, is escaped. See <a href="/docs/filters/strings/#safe-markup">Safe markup</a>.</p>

	{% apply example(context: { name: "<em>Ada</em>" }) %}
		{% verbatim %}
{% apply replace("NAME", name) %}
	<p>Hello, NAME</p>
{% endapply %}
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<p>A filter that returns a plain string, such as one of your own, has its result escaped like any other output. Return <a href="/docs/api/safe-markup/">safe markup</a> from it to keep the HTML. <code>apply</code> doesn't create a scope.</p>

	<p>This site uses <code>apply</code> with its own filters to highlight every code example.</p>
{% endblock %}
